  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eCMdH",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902402319,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Identity/Application/Command/RegisterUnder18CommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 52,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902402319",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`isDummyEmail` is computed via `email.Split('@').LastOrDefault()`, which treats malformed inputs like \"@U18.virgin.com\" (empty local part) or addresses with multiple '@' as valid dummy emails. That weakens the boundary check for “system-generated dummy email” and is inconsistent with the stricter dummy-email parsing used elsewhere (e.g., Member Management).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Tightened the Identity boundary validation to require exactly one @ separator with non-empty local and domain parts before comparing the configured dummy domain, so malformed addresses such as @U18.virgin.com and addresses containing multiple @ characters are rejected."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eCMd-",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902402410,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Loyalty.Identity/Application/Command/RegisterUnder18CommandHandler.cs",
      "line": 158,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902402410",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`PublishEmailEvent` inserts the WelcomeEmail event-store record but does not delete it if the Service Bus publish fails. Other Identity flows (e.g., RegisterCommandHandler/CompleteSignUpHandler) delete the event-store record on publish failure to avoid orphaned records and retry side-effects.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Wrapped welcome-email event insertion and Service Bus publication in the same compensation pattern as the customer and VRed/OCDB events, deleting the WelcomeEmail event-store record and rethrowing when insertion or publication fails."
    }
  ],
